#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# from_continued_fraction

#% text
# `from_continued_fraction(terms)` gives the number whose continued fraction has the given terms.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A finite list gives a rational number (or an expression, for symbolic terms). A final sublist is a repeating period and gives a quadratic irrational.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
from_continued_fraction([4, 2, 6, 7])
#% output
#= 415/93

#% cell
from_continued_fraction([1, [2]])
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)

#% cell
from_continued_fraction([1, [1]])
#% output
#= (1/2)*(1 + 5^(1/2))

#% cell
from_continued_fraction([a, b, c])
#% output
#= a + (b + c^-1)^-1

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A period after a non-repeating part:

#% cell
from_continued_fraction([3, [1, 2]])
#% output
#= 2 + 3^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The convergents of `sqrt(2)`:

#% cell
table(from_continued_fraction(prepend(table(2, k - 1), 1)), k, 6)
#% output
#= [1, 3/2, 7/5, 17/12, 41/29, 99/70]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The value of a periodic fraction, numerically:

#% cell
n(from_continued_fraction([2, [1, 1, 1, 4]])) - sqrt(7.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `continued_fraction`, `rationalize`
